{
  "id": "31748_rousuru",
  "headword": "{弄|ろう}する",
  "reading": "ろうする",
  "romaji": "rousuru",
  "part_of_speech": "suru verb",
  "gloss": "to resort to (tricks); to use (sophistry)",
  "definitions": [
    {
      "sense_number": 1,
      "gloss": "to resort to (tricks); to use (sophistry)",
      "explanation": "To make use of a scheme, a trick or clever words, usually to get one's way unfairly. Almost always critical."
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "id": "31748_rousuru_ex1",
      "japanese": "⟦{策|さく}→策：09997_saku⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{弄|ろう}する。",
      "english": "To resort to scheming.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "31748_rousuru_ex2",
      "japanese": "⟦{詭弁|きべん}→詭弁：21252_kiben⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{弄|ろう}して⟦{責任|せきにん}→責任：03298_sekinin⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧⟦{逃|のが}れた→逃れる：10425_nogareru⟧。",
      "english": "He evaded responsibility with sophistry.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "31748_rousuru_ex3",
      "japanese": "{小細工|こざいく}⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{弄|ろう}する⟦より→より：09476_yori⟧、⟦{正直|しょうじき}→正直：01562_shoujiki⟧⟦に→に：00314_ni⟧⟦{話|はな}した→話す：00467_hanasu⟧⟦ほうがいい→ほうがいい：10078_hougaii⟧。",
      "english": "Rather than resorting to petty tricks, it's better to speak honestly.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    }
  ],
  "notes": "A formal, written word. Its object is nearly always a noun for a scheme or for clever talk.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- ⟦{策|さく}→策：09997_saku⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{弄|ろう}する: to scheme\n- ⟦{詭弁|きべん}→詭弁：21252_kiben⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{弄|ろう}する: to use sophistry\n- {小細工|こざいく}⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{弄|ろう}する: to resort to petty tricks\n- ⟦{言葉|ことば}→言葉：02880_kotoba⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{弄|ろう}する: to play with words\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- ⟦{弄|もてあそ}ぶ→弄ぶ：12485_moteasobu⟧: to toy with; the same kanji as a native verb, used for playing with an object or with someone's feelings",
